Here \code{q = 1} for Erlang-1 clocks and \code{q = 2} for Erlang-2 clocks. In
\code{erlang_shape = "mixed"}, the clock is Erlang-1 with probability \code{omega} and
Erlang-2 otherwise, with both components having the same mean \code{mG} or \code{mK}.
The internal rates \code{lambda_g} and \code{lambda_k} are generated by the
\code{Ttransform}; they are not user-facing model parameters and should not be
put in a \code{design()} formula.

\code{erlang_type} selects which clocks are active. \code{"none"} has no clocks;
\code{"local_kill"} adds an independent kill clock to each accumulator;
\code{"global_kill"} adds one kill clock shared by all accumulators in a trial;
\code{"local_guess"} adds local guess clocks; and \code{"local_kill_guess"} adds both
local guess and local kill clocks. A kill clock that wins produces an
omission. A guess clock that wins is represented using the package's timed
